<% content_for :title, "Privacy Policy" %>
<article class="legal max-w-3xl space-y-5 text-ink-soft">
  <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink">Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="data text-xs">Version <%= OpenTrust::LEGAL_VERSION %> · Effective <%= OpenTrust::LEGAL_EFFECTIVE %></p>
  <nav aria-label="Contents" class="card text-sm"><p class="font-bold text-ink">Contents</p><ol class="mt-2 list-decimal space-y-1 pl-5"><li><a href="#p1" class="text-blue underline">Who is responsible</a></li><li><a href="#p2" class="text-blue underline">Whose data we handle</a></li><li><a href="#p3" class="text-blue underline">What we collect</a></li><li><a href="#p4" class="text-blue underline">Why we use it and on what basis</a></li><li><a href="#p5" class="text-blue underline">Who sees what</a></li><li><a href="#p6" class="text-blue underline">Who we share with</a></li><li><a href="#p7" class="text-blue underline">Accuracy: whose statements these are</a></li><li><a href="#p8" class="text-blue underline">How long we keep it</a></li><li><a href="#p9" class="text-blue underline">How we protect it</a></li><li><a href="#p10" class="text-blue underline">Your rights</a></li><li><a href="#p11" class="text-blue underline">Numbers recorded in error</a></li><li><a href="#p12" class="text-blue underline">Children</a></li><li><a href="#p13" class="text-blue underline">International transfers</a></li><li><a href="#p14" class="text-blue underline">Cookies</a></li><li><a href="#p15" class="text-blue underline">Changes to this policy</a></li><li><a href="#p16" class="text-blue underline">Grievance Officer and contact</a></li></ol></nav>
  <section id="p1"><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink">1. Who is responsible</h2><div class="mt-2 space-y-3"><p><%= OpenTrust::OPERATOR[:name] %>, <%= OpenTrust::OPERATOR[:address] %> (the "<strong>Operator</strong>") runs OpenTrust. For the purposes of the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 ("<strong>DPDP Act</strong>"), when and as it applies, the Operator is a data fiduciary for the data it decides how to use to run, secure and moderate the Service. For the content of Reports, the Merchant who submits a Report decides to share it, and is responsible for having a lawful basis and any notice or consent required; the Operator hosts and shows that content as an online intermediary.</p></div></section><section id="p2"><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink">2. Whose data we handle</h2><div class="mt-2 space-y-3"><ul class="list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5"><li><strong>Merchants</strong> who register and use the Service, and their authorised users.</li><li><strong>Individuals whose mobile numbers appear in Reports.</strong> They have no relationship with us and did not give us their numbers. Merchants did, so we explain below what we do with them.</li></ul></div></section><section id="p3"><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink">3. What we collect</h2><div class="mt-2 space-y-3"><p class="font-bold text-ink">From Merchants</p><ul class="list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5"><li>Registration details: your name, business name, website, GSTIN (optional), work email, mobile number and password (stored only as a one-way hash). Your mobile number is used to reach you about your account and is never shown to other Merchants.</li><li>Terms acceptance: time, version and IP address.</li><li>Usage: API key identifiers (never the key itself), when keys were last used, Check and request counts, and technical logs such as IP address and user agent.</li><li>Reports you submit and messages you send us.</li></ul><p class="mt-3 font-bold text-ink">About Individuals (in Reports and Checks)</p><ul class="list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5"><li>The mobile number, held as (a) a keyed cryptographic hash used for matching and (b) an encrypted copy readable only by authorised administrators for moderation and grievance handling, plus the last 4 digits.</li><li>The category of experience, an optional short note written by the Merchant, and dates. A Merchant may also say that a bank, payment gateway or law-enforcement body confirmed the activity, and add a private reference (such as a complaint number) that only OpenTrust administrators can see. Notes are screened to reject emails, links and phone numbers, but may still contain information we did not intend to receive. Tell us if you see any and we will remove it.</li><li>We do <strong>not</strong> ask Merchants for customer names, addresses, order or payment data.</li><li>Numbers that are only <em>checked</em> are not stored as such. We keep a count of Checks per Merchant, not a list of numbers checked.</li></ul></div></section><section id="p4"><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink">4. Why we use it and on what basis</h2><div class="mt-2 space-y-3"><div class="overflow-x-auto"><table class="w-full text-left text-sm"><thead class="text-ink"><tr><th class="py-2 pr-4">Purpose</th><th>Basis</th></tr></thead><tbody class="divide-y divide-ink/20"><tr><td class="py-2 pr-4">Registering, approving and supporting Merchants; providing the API and portal</td><td>Merchant's consent and our agreement with them</td></tr><tr><td class="py-2 pr-4">Letting Merchants share and look up experiences with numbers, to help them avoid repeat fraud and abuse</td><td>A legitimate use recognised by law, namely preventing and detecting fraud and abuse, and consent where the law requires it</td></tr><tr><td class="py-2 pr-4">Security, abuse prevention, moderation, handling complaints and defending legal claims</td><td>Legal obligations and legitimate uses as permitted by law</td></tr><tr><td class="py-2 pr-4">Complying with law and responding to lawful requests</td><td>Legal obligation</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>We do not sell personal data, show advertising, build advertising profiles or allow bulk export.</p></div></section><section id="p5"><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink">5. Who sees what</h2><div class="mt-2 space-y-3"><ul class="list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5"><li><strong>Other approved Merchants</strong> who check a number see the last 4 digits, how many Merchants reported it, and for each Report the category, note and date, and whom the Merchant says confirmed it (if anyone), marked as from a verified Merchant. They never see the full number or the name of the reporting Merchant.</li><li><strong>Authorised administrators</strong> can see full numbers and reporting Merchants, only to run, moderate and secure the Service and handle complaints. Admin actions are logged.</li><li>Every Result carries a notice that Reports are unverified observations and not a finding about anyone.</li></ul></div></section><section id="p6"><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink">6. Who we share with</h2><div class="mt-2 space-y-3"><p>We share data only with: (a) service providers who process it for us under written terms (for example hosting, and email delivery through Resend); (b) courts, regulators, law-enforcement and other authorities where we believe in good faith that the law or a lawful order requires it, or to protect rights, safety or the Service; (c) professional advisers, insurers and auditors under duties of confidence; and (d) a successor in a merger, acquisition or restructuring, who must honour this policy. We do not otherwise disclose the identity of reporting Merchants.</p></div></section><section id="p7"><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink">7. Accuracy: whose statements these are</h2><div class="mt-2 space-y-3"><p>Reports are statements made by Merchants. We do not verify them and do not state or warrant that any of them is accurate, complete or lawful, and we are not responsible for their content. Where something is wrong, our process below exists to correct or remove it. Our responsibility for Merchant Content is governed by the Terms of Use, which also limit our liability.</p></div></section><section id="p8"><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink">8. How long we keep it</h2><div class="mt-2 space-y-3"><ul class="list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5"><li>Reports: 5 years from submission, after which they are deleted or irreversibly anonymised, unless needed for an open complaint, legal claim or legal requirement. Reports removed by an administrator, or withdrawn by the merchant who shared them, are deleted after 90 days.</li><li>Merchant account data: while the account is active and 3 years afterwards for legal and audit purposes.</li><li>Technical logs: 90 days. Audit logs of admin actions: 3 years.</li><li>We may keep any data for longer where we reasonably need it to establish, exercise or defend legal claims, prevent fraud or abuse of the Service, or comply with law.</li></ul></div></section><section id="p9"><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink">9. How we protect it</h2><div class="mt-2 space-y-3"><p>We use reasonable security practices appropriate to the data: keyed hashing and field-level encryption for numbers, hashed passwords and API keys, encrypted connections, role-based admin access with audit logging, and rate limiting. No system is completely secure and we do not promise that ours cannot be breached. If a personal data breach affects you we will notify the Data Protection Board of India and affected persons as the law requires.</p></div></section><section id="p10"><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink">10. Your rights</h2><div class="mt-2 space-y-3"><p>Subject to Applicable Law, you may ask for a summary of the personal data we hold about you and how it is processed; ask us to correct, complete or update it; ask us to erase it; seek grievance redressal; and nominate another person to exercise your rights if you die or become incapacitated. Where processing rests on consent you may withdraw it at any time, without affecting what was done before. Write to <span class="data"><%= OpenTrust::GRIEVANCE_EMAIL %></span>. We may need to verify who you are, and will respond within 30 days. We may decline or limit a request where the law allows, for example where it cannot be verified, is manifestly unfounded or excessive, or would prejudice the prevention or detection of fraud, the rights of others, or the establishment or defence of legal claims, and we will tell you why. If you are not satisfied you may approach the Data Protection Board of India once it is constituted.</p></div></section><section id="p11"><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink">11. Numbers recorded in error</h2><div class="mt-2 space-y-3"><p>If you believe a number of yours was recorded in error, or a note about you is inaccurate, write to the Grievance Officer from the number concerned, or otherwise show that you control it, and say why. Because numbers are stored as hashes, we can find matching Reports from the number you give us. We will review the Report, may ask the reporting Merchant to substantiate it without disclosing your identity to them beyond what is necessary, and will remove or correct it where we think it is not justified. Our decision is made in our reasonable discretion, and we will tell you the outcome.</p></div></section><section id="p12"><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink">12. Children</h2><div class="mt-2 space-y-3"><p>The Service is for businesses and is not directed at children. Merchants must not submit Reports about numbers they know belong to a child. If we learn that one has, we will remove it.</p></div></section><section id="p13"><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink">13. International transfers</h2><div class="mt-2 space-y-3"><p>We aim to store data in India. If a provider processes data outside India, we will do so only where the law permits and with appropriate safeguards.</p></div></section><section id="p14"><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink">14. Cookies</h2><div class="mt-2 space-y-3"><p>We use a single first-party session cookie to keep Merchants and administrators logged in and to protect forms against forgery. We do not use advertising or third-party tracking cookies. Our pages load fonts from Google Fonts, which may receive your IP address.</p></div></section><section id="p15"><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink">15. Changes to this policy</h2><div class="mt-2 space-y-3"><p>We may update this policy at any time and will change the version and date above. We will tell registered Merchants about material changes by email or in the Service. Using the Service after the effective date means you accept the update.</p></div></section><section id="p16"><h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-ink">16. Grievance Officer and contact</h2><div class="mt-2 space-y-3"><p>Grievance Officer: <strong><%= OpenTrust::GRIEVANCE_OFFICER[:name] %></strong>, <%= OpenTrust::GRIEVANCE_OFFICER[:designation] %>, <%= OpenTrust::GRIEVANCE_OFFICER[:address] %>. Email: <span class="data"><%= OpenTrust::GRIEVANCE_EMAIL %></span>. We acknowledge complaints within 24 hours and aim to resolve them within 15 days. General enquiries: <span class="data"><%= OpenTrust::FEEDBACK_EMAIL %></span>.</p></div></section>
</article>
